Subject: [PATCH 0/5] Base lab-process-mail work on LAB_BASE_BRANCH
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

lab-process-mail based every pass on trunk. That suits an ordinary
contributor, but lab-claude is Pat's own assistant and should see the
tree he works in, which is b/dev. The last patch reads the base from
LAB_BASE_BRANCH, a jj revset that defaults to trunk(), so

    LAB_BASE_BRANCH=b/dev@upstream lab-process-mail

rebases unmerged work onto b/dev, creates the pass workspace there,
and tells the agent its base so the prompt's steps follow it. The
series still applies to trunk. When b/dev is rebuilt upstream, work on
it follows the new head and the old b/dev commits are dropped rather
than copied; a test covers that case.

Patches 1-4 are the lab-process-mail commits as they stand on b/dev,
included for context. They are patches 1-4 of "[PATCH 0/6] Answer
the inbox with lab-process-mail" [1]. Only patch 5 is new.

[1] id:cover.1792003466.git.claude@p7x.dev

claude (5):
  src/lab-process-mail: Answer the inbox from outside the tree
  src/lab-process-mail: Package it and install under ~/local
  src/lab-process-mail: Keep rebased work on its prerequisites
  src/lab-process-mail: Run each pass in its own workspace
  src/lab-process-mail: Take the base from LAB_BASE_BRANCH

